WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.050
You want to find new customers, but first you have to search and filter again. Which companies

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:12.100
fit your offer? In BelgoBase, start by explaining your business. Let's take a look.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:17.333
I deliver fruit at work and want to find companies in Mechelen. BelgoBase suggests possible

00:00:17.333 --> 00:00:22.567
target groups. We make it concrete: postcode 2800, with at least twenty full-time-equivalent

00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:27.800
employees.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:34.775
The assistant asks for clarification. It can use workforce size; I must judge actual presence

00:00:34.775 --> 00:00:41.750
at the office. We confirm the criteria. The proposal contains 239 companies.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:49.275
I click Find these companies. This is the real selection, with company names, locations and

00:00:49.275 --> 00:00:56.800
available figures. These are the results of our search, not invented examples.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:02.850
Contact research is available as a separate step. For this demonstration, we first download the

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:08.900
company list. One click and BelgoBase prepares the Excel file.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:16.450
This is the content of the downloaded file: 239 companies with the available data. A concrete

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:24.000
selection to review and use for your next prospecting round.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:31.550
What could BelgoBase find for your business? Request a demo with your own question. Already

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:39.100
have many Excel lists? Watch the next video to see how you can combine and clean them up.
